ery belonging to `cat` has calculated these relevance scores against the Keys of all three tokens. The higher the score, the stronger the matching signal. But these scores are not probabilities yet.\n\nWe need another operation.\n\n## Scaling the attention scores\n\nBefore applying Softmax, we divide the scores by the square root of the Key dimension.\n\nThe formula:\n\n$$ ScaledScores = \\frac{QK^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} $$\n\nHere:\n\n$$ d_k = \\text{dimension of each Key vector} $$\n\nWhy do we divide by $\\sqrt{d_k}$? \n\nBecause when the vector dimensions become large, dot products can become very large. Large values can make Softmax produce extremely concentrated probabilities, resulting in very small gradients. Scaling helps stabilize the values.\n\nFor example, if:\n\n$$ d_k = 64 $$\n\nThen:\n\n$$ \\sqrt{64}=8 $$\n\nSo we divide every attention score by 8.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Scale attention scores\nscaled_scores = attention_scores / math.sqrt(d_model)\n\nprint(\"Scaled attention scores:\")\nprint(scaled_scores)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T17:26:19.683883Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T17:26:19.684336Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T17:26:19.69832Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T17:26:19.684308Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T17:26:19.69731Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Scaled attention scores:\ntensor([[[ 5.6566e-02, -1.1155e-01,  1.8898e-01,  1.3067e-01,  2.3296e-01,\n          -1.0343e-01,  6.9149e-01,  2.3535e-01,  3.3952e-01, -2.3945e-01,\n          -1.9823e-01],\n         [ 2.1485e-01, -2.2010e-01,  1.6758e-01,  4.0609e-01,  1.1342e-01,\n          -4.1737e-01,  7.4680e-02, -1.1418e-01, -1.6909e-01, -3.0947e-02,\n           2.7097e-01],\n         [-3.2430e-02, -1.6065e-01, -8.5297e-02, -2.1916e-01, -1.2522e-01,\n          -2.5364e-01, -9.2035e-02, -1.6096e-01, -9.5643e-02, -2.3493e-01,\n          -6.1902e-02],\n         [ 4.5528e-01,  2.2858e-01,  1.0189e+